From 8224e8c44e7e628328bd5ecdf426aa0e9323e79b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OneFeiFan <3022504358@qq.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 22:41:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] gki_defconfig: drop the redundant MODULE_SIG=n line

The AOSP GKI base already leaves MODULE_SIG disabled; the explicit =n
was a no-op. The generated .config is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/configs/gki_defconfig | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/gki_defconfig b/arch/arm64/configs/gki_defconfig
index ac8aefafa..d7a15d148 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/gki_defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/gki_defconfig
@@ -869,7 +869,6 @@ CONFIG_NTSYNC=y
 # Phase 10.4: ZRAM LZ4K/LZ4KD with ARM64 NEON.
 CONFIG_ZSMALLOC=y
 CONFIG_ZRAM=y
-CONFIG_MODULE_SIG=n
 CONFIG_CRYPTO_LZO=y
 CONFIG_ZRAM_DEF_COMP_LZ4=y
 CONFIG_CRYPTO_LZ4HC=y
